   "source": [
    "# 🧠 RepoLens — CampusX Corrective RAG (CRAG) Agent\n",
    "**Implementation based on the official CampusX CRAG Architecture & Paper (Yan et al.)**\n",
    "\n",
    "### 🏛️ Core CRAG Stages:\n",
    "1. **Retrieve**: Pulls top codebase chunks from FAISS.\n",
    "2. **Document Evaluator (`eval_each_doc`)**:\n",
    "   - Scores each document from `0.0` to `1.0`.\n",
    "   - Calculates overall verdict using thresholds (`UPPER_TH = 0.7`, `LOWER_TH = 0.3`):\n",
    "     - 🟢 **CORRECT** (`score >= 0.7`): Code retrieval is accurate ➔ decompose & refine strips ➔ generate.\n",
    "     - 🔴 **INCORRECT** (`score < 0.3`): Irrelevant ➔ rewrite query ➔ Web/fallback search ➔ generate.\n",
    "     - 🟡 **AMBIGUOUS** (`0.3 <= score < 0.7`): Partially relevant ➔ combine internal code strips + external search ➔ generate.\n",
    "3. **Knowledge Strip Decomposition (`refine`)**: Decomposes code into fine-grained strips and discards noise.\n",
    "4. **Query Rewriter (`rewrite_query`)**: Rewrites user questions into optimal keywords.\n",
    "5. **Web Search / External Fallback (`web_search`)**: Uses Tavily Search API or fallback expansion.\n",
    "6. **Grounded Generation (`generate`)**: Synthesizes the final answer with citations."
   ]
  },
  {
